{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBFibreExtension","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBFibreExtension","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.extension_mul_conj_on_axis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.extension_mul_conj_on_axis","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBFibreExtension.lean#L80-L84","doc":"**σ-unitarity transfers to the axis values of any extension (derived).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.extension_ne_zero_on_axis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.extension_ne_zero_on_axis","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBFibreExtension.lean#L69-L78","doc":"**No zeros on the real axis (derived).**  The constructed `phiB` is a\nunimodular phase, so any extension is nonvanishing on `ℝ` — the zero\nlattice of a genuine Faddeev extension is strictly off-axis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.offAxis_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.offAxis_bridge","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBFibreExtension.lean#L57-L67","doc":"**Off-axis bridge (derived).**  Quasi-periodicity pins the extension on\nthe `+ib`-shifted line in terms of the CONSTRUCTED `phiB` values on the\nreal axis: the identification is rigid along the `b`-lattice, not free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBFibreExtension.faddeev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBFibreExtension.faddeev","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBFibreExtension.lean#L53-L53","doc":"(ii) It satisfies the Faddeev modular-double shift equations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBFibreExtension.extends_phiB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBFibreExtension.extends_phiB","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBFibreExtension.lean#L51-L51","doc":"(i) It restricts to the constructed real integral on the real axis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBFibreExtension.Φ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBFibreExtension.Φ","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBFibreExtension.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The extension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBFibreExtension.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBFibreExtension.mk","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBFibreExtension.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBFibreExtension","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBFibreExtension","kind":"class","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/PhiBFibreExtension.lean#L40-L53","doc":"**The def↔contour identification (§3b conjecture class).**  The\nconstructed real-integral `phiB b` extends to a full Faddeev `Φ_b` on the\nfibre branch: a function `Φ : ℂ → ℂ` that (i) restricts to `phiB b` on\nthe real axis and (ii) satisfies the two modular-double shift equations.\nThe open content is the analytic continuation; no instance is fabricated.\n(`0 < b` puts the real `b` in `FaddeevPhi`'s `Re b > 0` scope.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}